.TH COF-TRUST 1 "2026-11-13" "cof 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cof-trust \- Trust a project config file, or consent to an orchestration
document's capabilities. A .yml/.yaml PATH is a document (shows the
capabilities it needs and asks); anything else is a project config file (shows
what it sets and asks)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
cof trust [OPTIONS] [path]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Trusts a project config file, or consents to an orchestration document's
capabilities. A .yml/.yaml PATH is a document (shows the capabilities it needs
and asks); anything else is a project config file (shows what it sets and
asks). Trust applies until the file's content changes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B PATH
Config file or .yml/.yaml orchestration document to trust (default:
circuitry.config.json or config.json in the current directory).
.TP
.B --yes, -y
Trust without asking.
.TP
.B --list
List trusted files and whether each still matches.
.TP
.B --config, -c
\fICONFIG\fR Config to resolve library sources from, for a .yml/.yaml
document's use: ref: children (or use CIRCUITRY_CONFIG).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B cof trust
Trusts circuitry.config.json or config.json in the current directory.
.TP
.B cof trust my-flow.yml
Shows and consents to a document's capabilities.
.TP
.B cof trust --list
Lists every trusted file and whether it still matches.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_CONFIG
Used to resolve a document's use: ref: library sources, when trusting a
document.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/trusted.json
Where every trust decision is recorded.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed, or the input was invalid.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error -- an unrecognized option or missing argument.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcof(1)\fR, \fBcof-untrust(1)\fR, \fBcof-run(1)\fR
